# CICD Check

Runs pre-release sanity checks on a Node.js project and prints a pass/fail report
This tool was developed in Ubuntu.

Requirements

Bash 4+, git, node, npm, docker.

Usage

    ./cicd-check.sh all [repo-path]    # run all checks (default: current dir)
    ./cicd-check.sh help               # show this README
    ./cicd-check.sh version            # show version

Checks

- Required tools are installed
- Working directory is clean
- On `main`, `master` or `release`
- `npm audit` and `npm ci` report 0 vulnerabilities
- `npm test` passes
- Node version matches `.nvmrc` and `package.json` engines
- Dockerfile passes `docker build --check`

Note: `npm ci` reinstalls `node_modules`, and the script always exits 0.
